IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vmu-nouns`
IMPORT `vmu-time`
IMPORT `vmu-s04-s05-values`

-- Sections 11 and 12.
-- Section 11 states the values of the fee unit and the penalty unit and the annual rate for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012, "Despite sections 5 and 6".
-- For any other financial year the answer is the one section 5 gives.
-- Section 12 says that "Nothing in the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 applies" to the fixing of a unit or an annual rate under section 5 or 11.

§ `Section 11 -- Provisions for 2012 to 2013`

-- Subsection (2) treats a reference to the value "calculated in accordance with section 5(3)" as a reference to the value in subsection (1), for that year:
-- the same function answers both.
-- src:119 | (1) Despite sections 5 and 6, for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012—
-- src:120 | (a) the value of a fee unit is $12.53; and
-- src:121 | (b) the value of a penalty unit is $140.84.
-- src:122 | (2) Any reference in this Act or any other Act or statutory rule to the value of a fee unit or penalty unit calculated in accordance with section 5(3) is to be treated for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012 as a reference to the value of a fee unit or penalty unit as provided by subsection (1).
@ref s 11(1)(a), s 11(2) (src:119-122)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the Treasurer fixed an amount for the financial year by notice published in the Government Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount fixed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 11(1)(a) -- the value of a fee unit for the financial year, with section 11(2)` MEANS
    IF `s 11 -- the financial year is the one commencing on 1 July 2012` year
    THEN JUST `s 11(1)(a) -- the value of a fee unit for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012, in dollars`
    ELSE `s 5(1) -- the value of a fee unit for the financial year` `the Treasurer fixed an amount for the financial year by notice published in the Government Gazette` `the amount fixed`

-- src:119 | (1) Despite sections 5 and 6, for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012—
-- src:120 | (a) the value of a fee unit is $12.53; and
-- src:121 | (b) the value of a penalty unit is $140.84.
-- src:122 | (2) Any reference in this Act or any other Act or statutory rule to the value of a fee unit or penalty unit calculated in accordance with section 5(3) is to be treated for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012 as a reference to the value of a fee unit or penalty unit as provided by subsection (1).
@ref s 11(1)(b), s 11(2) (src:119-122)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the Treasurer fixed an amount for the financial year by notice published in the Government Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount fixed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 11(1)(b) -- the value of a penalty unit for the financial year, with section 11(2)` MEANS
    IF `s 11 -- the financial year is the one commencing on 1 July 2012` year
    THEN JUST `s 11(1)(b) -- the value of a penalty unit for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012, in dollars`
    ELSE `s 5(2) -- the value of a penalty unit for the financial year` `the Treasurer fixed an amount for the financial year by notice published in the Government Gazette` `the amount fixed`

-- Subsection (4) treats a reference to the annual rate fixed under section 5(4) for that year as a reference to the rate in subsection (3):
-- the same function answers both. For any other financial year, section 5(5) decides.
-- src:123 | (3) Despite section 5, the annual rate for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012 is taken to be 2⋅5%.
-- src:124 | (4) Any reference in this Act or any other Act or statutory rule to the annual rate fixed in accordance with section 5(4) for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012 is to be treated as a reference to the annual rate as provided by subsection (3).
@ref s 11(3), s 11(4) (src:123-124)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the annual rate fixed under subsection (4) for the financial year` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the annual rate that was determined for the previous financial year` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 11(3) -- the annual rate for the financial year, with section 11(4)` MEANS
    IF `s 11 -- the financial year is the one commencing on 1 July 2012` year
    THEN JUST `s 11(3) -- the annual rate for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012`
    ELSE `s 5(5) -- the annual rate for the financial year` `the annual rate fixed under subsection (4) for the financial year` `the annual rate that was determined for the previous financial year`

-- "Despite sections 5 and 6" the values for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012 are the ones stated; the text does not say whether a notice is still due before 1 June of that year.
-- For 2012 the last day is therefore NOTHING; for any other financial year it is the last day section 6 gives.
-- src:119 | (1) Despite sections 5 and 6, for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012—
@ref s 11(1) (src:119)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 11(1) -- the last day on which notice of the values may be published, for the financial year` MEANS
    IF `s 11 -- the financial year is the one commencing on 1 July 2012` year
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`s 6 -- the last day on which notice may be published in the year` year)

-- "Despite section 5, the annual rate for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012 is taken to be 2⋅5%": the text does not say whether it is still to be fixed before 1 March of that year.
-- src:123 | (3) Despite section 5, the annual rate for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012 is taken to be 2⋅5%.
@ref s 11(3) (src:123)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 11(3) -- the last day on which the annual rate may be fixed, for the financial year` MEANS
    IF `s 11 -- the financial year is the one commencing on 1 July 2012` year
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`s 5(4) -- the last day on which the annual rate for the financial year commencing on 1 July in the year may be fixed` year)

§ `Section 12 -- Subordinate Legislation Act 1994`

-- "Nothing in the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 applies to the fixing of— (a) a fee or penalty unit in accordance with section 5 or 11; or (b) an annual rate in accordance with section 5 or 11."
-- A flat negative: for the fixings it names, the Act does not apply, JUST FALSE. For any other fixing, or one not made under section 5 or 11, the text says neither yes nor no, so NOTHING.
-- src:127 | Nothing in the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 applies to the fixing of—
-- src:128 | (a) a fee or penalty unit in accordance with section 5 or 11; or
-- src:129 | (b) an annual rate in accordance with section 5 or 11.
@ref s 12 (src:127-129)
GIVEN `what is fixed` IS A `Thing fixed`
      `it is fixed in accordance with section 5 or 11` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12 -- the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 applies to the fixing` MEANS
    IF `the fixing is one of those that section 12 names` AND `it is fixed in accordance with section 5 or 11`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the fixing is one of those that section 12 names` MEANS
            CONSIDER `what is fixed`
            WHEN `a fee unit` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a penalty unit` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `an annual rate` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `something else` THEN FALSE
